are a recognizable conceptual system while using genuinely different compositions. Simple palette swaps or the same layout in three containers are not enough.\n\n## Art direction\n\nChoose the visual concept, typography strategy, palette, rendering medium, motifs, transitions, and interaction behavior yourself. Take a clear creative position. Avoid familiar startup aesthetics, generic dark dashboards, glass cards, decorative gradient blobs, and interchangeable component-library layouts unless you radically transform them into something specific to this identity.\n\nUse only graphics generated by the application itself. You may use HTML, CSS, SVG, Canvas 2D, or WebGL, but do not load external images, fonts, videos, libraries, APIs, or other network assets. System fonts are allowed.\n\n## Experience requirements\n\n- The current expression must fill the experience and remain visually dominant.\n- Switching expressions must feel like entering another manifestation of the same identity.\n- Preserve every exact piece of supplied event content somewhere legible in the experience.\n- Make the Poster composition readable at a 4:5 aspect ratio and present it elegantly inside wider screens.\n- Make the Motion timeline deterministic and independent of display refresh rate.\n- Make the Instrument respond immediately to pointer and touch input.\n- Include a seed control or a small set of seed variations that remain recognizably part of the same identity family.\n- Handle desktop, narrow mobile, high-DPI displays, keyboard focus, and `prefers-reduced-motion` gracefully.\n- Keep the console free of avoidable errors.\n\n## Deterministic interface\n\nExpose `window.__LIVING_IDENTITY__` with callable methods:\n\n- `reset(seed)` 鈂200\224 restore the entire experience with the supplied integer seed;\n- `setMode(name)` 鈂200\224 accept `poster`, `motion`, or `instrument`;\n- `seek(milliseconds)` 鈂200\224 place the Motion sequence at an exact time from 0 through 12000;\n- `snapshot()` 鈂200\224 return a JSON-safe summary containing seed, mode, motion time, play state, and the meaningful state of the interactive composition;\n- `runSelfTest()` 鈂200\224 exercise the real state functions and return `{ passed, tests }`, with a name, boolean pass value, and short detail for every check.\n\nAt minimum, the self-test must verify deterministic reset, all three modes, exact Motion seeking, the 12-second timeline boundary, and finite numeric state after interaction.\n\n## Technical constraints\n\n- Create exactly one complete `index.html` file.\n- Put all markup, styles, rendering, animation, interaction, and logic in that file.\n- The file must open directly in a modern browser without a server or build step.\n- Do not use external dependencies or network requests.\n- Use a seeded pseudo-random generator for every identity-affecting variation.\n- Cap animation deltas and do not let tab suspension corrupt the timeline.\n- Every visible control must work.\n\n## Quality bar\n\nThe finished result should feel like a renowned independent design studio, motion designer, creative coder, and interaction designer built one small but complete cultural identity together. It should reward close inspection, but the concept and difference between the three expressions should be obvious within fifteen seconds.\n\nBuild the experience directly. Make the creative decisions yourself, run one concise validation pass, fix blocking failures, and keep the final response brief.\n\nWork only inside the current working directory.\n\nUse pnpm exclusively if dependency installation or package scripts are needed. Do not use npm.\nSet the browser title and the primary visible title to your model name, using only identity information already available to you. Add nothing else to either title.\nRun the relevant checks yourself. Do not edit files outside the current working directory.' 
